  "target_phenomenon": "admission-control value under genuine overload",
  "hypothesis": "Arrival rate exceeds sustainable throughput, so not every request can meet its SLO regardless of policy -- ordering determines WHICH requests succeed. NOTE (confirmed finding, see the design doc): oracle_srtf is NOT guaranteed ANWG-optimal here -- it is a hindsight shortest-job-first ceiling (optimal for mean flow time), and can actually score below fifo under this repo's priority-weighted, deadline-based ANWG objective when it starves an early, otherwise-feasible request in favor of a stream of short ones.",
